(H/'template-extraction.md').write_text('''# Extracted backbone and slots

Each task supplies one explicit elementary curve and a concrete point on it, then requests the intersection of its normal with a stated axis. The five ordered operative stages are differentiation (with root/reciprocal power rewrites), evaluation at the actual supplied abscissa, negative reciprocal, point-slope normal equation and its expansion, and substitution of the other coordinate as zero. The final conclusion is a complete coordinate point. The precise original prompts, every solution stage, field placeholders, all complete bank values, correct links and any captured feedback are preserved in source-cases.json. extraction.json maps every original choice to its field and explicit expression recipe. There is no invented learner-error feedback.

Raw original replay has exact captured attributes and bytes, including missing fields and records. observed_served applies only the shared math-format normalization and regenerated field-owned IDs. The q-342222 repair adds one canonical math answer per existing blank, x=2 and y=0, derived independently from its printed fourth-root curve and normal. It supplies no other attributes and is separately documented as a repair. q-10878 and q-71542 stay raw-only because their response contracts are absent; normal APIs fail closed for them. All complete source questions have normalized replay. Later non-MA questions are replayed and audited separately.

Conservative authored slots: scale is a positive integer 1..8; the curve's existing terms and exponent structure stay fixed. Easy normal families are q-10871 (quadratic plus linear), q-342200 (constant minus quadratic), and q-342201 (quadratic plus linear plus constant). Their allowed abscissas are respectively 1,2,3; 1,2,3; and 0,2,3, keeping derivatives nonzero. Moderate root families use square inputs 1,4,9, cube inputs 1,8,27, fourth-power inputs 1,16,81; reciprocal input is 1,2,4. Hard uses canonical 2 sqrt(x)-4x, scaled together, at square inputs 1,4,9. This introduces no product/quotient/chain differentiation, implicit equations, or new line-solving method.

The target-axis slot is x or y at each level, with comparable one-equation arithmetic. Both coordinates, all axis mentions, the zero-coordinate substitution, conclusion, and answer records derive from this one slot. Radio gives a whole point; blank gives the two coordinate fragments, reflecting the observed contracts. These radio/blank extensions are authoring policies, not additional observed source contracts. Families and parameter choices within a band are unordered variations, with no progression.

Normal authored radio uses one complete five-line operation-error profile: the correct normal y=n(x-p)+y0, the tangent y=m(x-p)+y0, the positive-reciprocal line y=(1/m)(x-p)+y0, the normal with omitted abscissa shift y=n*x+y0, and the normal with omitted ordinate y=n(x-p). Here m is computed from the actual printed curve at p and n=-1/m. For the requested x-axis, each complete line is solved at y=0; for the y-axis, each is evaluated at x=0. These are authored inferred misconception/operation patterns, not original source banks or proven learner diagnoses. The entire five-member profile is rejected if any options coincide or any distractor equals the correct intercept. There is no offset fallback, option pool, or partial-bank repair. All rejected domain tuples remain listed in capacity.json; the blank catalog still serves the underlying valid mathematical task. Observed-bank profiles are separate: original abscissa/axis stay fixed while scale varies 1..8, retaining each source's full five-recipe bank. Scale-one mathematical banks match the original options and correct designation. No bank is pooled across originals.

Domains: root families are restricted to x>0 (including cube roots as a conservative positive branch); reciprocal uses x!=0; polynomial curves use real x. The curve-domain restriction concerns the point and derivative, not the extended normal line's intercept. Every declared point, both targets and both field shapes are exercised exhaustively, together with every scale and all valid complete bank profiles. Rendered structure retains the same five stages and actual operator operands, evaluation inputs and intermediate equations. No new plots are needed.
''')
